 <div class="dmNewParagraph" id="1372670427" style="margin-block-start:1em;margin-block-end:1em;transition:opacity 1s ease-in-out 0s;padding-top:0px;padding-bottom:0px;" data-blog-template="bind-author" data-diy-text="">May 17, 2022</div> 
 <div class="dmRespRow u_1471232539 blog-post-row" id="1471232539"> <div class="dmRespColsWrapper" id="1292474755"> <div class="dmRespCol large-12 medium-12 small-12 u_1668470589" id="1668470589"> <h3 class="dmNewParagraph" data-element-type="paragraph" id="1700776665" style="transition: opacity 1s ease-in-out 0s;">On Agricultural Land Use and Remote Sensing <div><br/></div> 
</h3> <div class="u_1750185103 imageWidget align-center" data-element-type="image" data-widget-type="image" id="1750185103"><img src="https://le-cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/dms3rep/multi/opt/IMG_20211013_170652-05e6dfca-1920w.jpg?Expires=1655386396&Signature=YHsZOQkBwjseZ4jBVsxPLHGPBkbza9KGiVST3O1hxNVh07FxnDkXyTzMwNb011LEugS-~0kBVL5tposjBiBwGDtY4Vw1EyHDqT9Rox1yXvOvoeB9s6ohkAm7GOYT-NkA3g32buYLZ7hOJLcaMWoQYYI3G6wjRyGOIYF-GOkj5qKC8kH~8cpaXfufLy1sQh0Q4BoioeJLlf83w11MiRbc35HDO1FoP8S7lBf~yVqMjzQGOxFGuYue7oJjWUDLBceQzm2fD3GtP~wpEeG5zcj2har6oLwo4WHu4or13Fy9QtOeIJzqwgcd3N8Z8To5jCCJPOPG-HeOjf-aIaHh8lbhlw__&Key-Pair-Id=K2NXBXLF010TJW" id="1129580552" class="" data-dm-image-path="https://cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/dms3rep/multi/IMG_20211013_170652-05e6dfca.jpg" width="1920" height="1085" onerror="handleImageLoadError(this)"/></div> 
 <div class="u_1250789679 dmNewParagraph" data-element-type="paragraph" id="1250789679" style="transition: none 0s ease 0s; display: block;">Kazakhstan &copy; HNEE 2022 / Henryk Alff</div> <div class="dmNewParagraph" data-element-type="paragraph" data-version="5" id="1361465275"><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p class="text-align-center m-size-19 size-24"><a href="https://cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/files/uploaded/Call%2520for%2520Applications%2520WHK%2520Remote%2520Sensing.pdf?Expires=1655386396&Signature=bjZZKUtP~Ov8VFRcRrmWW3bkMkYtphRB9pWrJo7kTH3U8~w4Qs1JVr0LLmKbpTI4D9YsNPqkbMJTXlp5h8xDeAACK~0bCH5KFX7LMCB8pGQ-N9OOOnpyJ4OHXvJKcyDaImrDR1NJBYwi~SXOAA9gVwkPjla~togp0KfR-15GZUnZcMtYzo0qfZOUd3y5etZJ-MiaFbTTuEnNGVjfrsDae3FADt8niFOCy9tI3eLqrHrVe4gNSNTI7XcGwqX9cjXaJMha6QTO4V6SZlom6TKqth3jaScPuQX0aKEwy51l6n9gzKAcWQMTBvnRXwFsj~WvjZ-FTJcUjl5HGIEnOqplfw__&Key-Pair-Id=K2NXBXLF010TJW" target="_blank" runtime_url="https://cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/files/uploaded/Call%2520for%2520Applications%2520WHK%2520Remote%2520Sensing.pdf" file="true" type="file" class="font-size-24 m-font-size-19" style="display: unset;">&gt;&gt; Download Call for Application as PDF &lt;&lt;</a><span style="display: initial;"><br/><br/><br/></span><a href="https://cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/files/uploaded/Call%2520for%2520app%2520fellow%25202e.pdf?Expires=1655386396&Signature=PaxAPIgPSYu46GwY0kb0ddQr~huujoi02-NfyVyPpZ3WtnAv6bIT9LF3P8dSuK6mE9zloYZ3KRvmG-3eJmGJ1rZb8WwRvy91UCJ~sLa7qIXKnNi0P6ytdn4eMPuajtK7TQQAiZTtwETW4z1A~l2z7ifEbbGkIjH6RXBGrVoUMQ6ZaJLPuLSPeuU~yuIjyUCN4Ox8xYOENA7-c8kbpl2bAOPAq6X49lxnGJ-Wr7wrL4~peJEH-XMMXyL5y7oUouGLlXJd4IqlIWyNg2gQwJKKpH9BOR6C-DBOG-22zRWvkEzKkNU9aDcgk4wVLE1TA-po5IXZMkKb4aX2cH1C4Q~ixA__&Key-Pair-Id=K2NXBXLF010TJW" target="_blank" runtime_url="https://cdn.website-editor.net/s/95ee33f6d4e04c8bae6d20897b80f304/files/uploaded/Call%2520for%2520app%2520fellow%25202e.pdf" file="true" type="file" style="display: initial;"><br/><br/></a></p></div> 
 <div class="dmNewParagraph" data-element-type="paragraph" data-version="5" id="1024081288"><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p class="size-24 m-size-19"><span class="font-size-24 m-font-size-19" style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">Student Assistant on Agricultural Land Use and Remote Sensing&nbsp;</span><span class="m-font-size-14 font-size-18" style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span class="m-font-size-14 font-size-18" style="font-weight: normal; display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="m-size-14 size-18"><span class="m-font-size-14 font-size-18" style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">Postgraduate (M.Sc. or M.A. student), 6 months, ca. 40h per month,&nbsp;<br/>from July 1</span><sup class="m-font-size-14 font-size-18" style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">st</sup><span class="m-font-size-14 font-size-18" style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">, 2022; (with the possibility of a 6 months extension)</span></p><p><br/></p><p style="line-height: 9.9pt;"><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span class="" style="display: unset;"><span style="display: unset;">The Student Assistant will work with the Junior Research Group TRANSECT (Agrarian Transformations and Social-Ecological Complexities - Local Bioeconomy Scenarios in Central and South Asia) funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF) at Eberswalde University for Sustainable Development (HNE Eberswalde, Germany). The Junior Research Group investigates the social-ecological effects and interdependencies of agrarian transformations in Central and South Asia.</span> 
</span></p><p><span style="display: unset;">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="display: unset;">Within the project, the Student Assistant will be concerned with mapping agricultural land cover, using remote sensing data (e.g. Sentinel-2 and Landsat 8). Primary duties include, but are not limited to:</span></p><p><span style="display: unset;">&nbsp;</span></p> <ul class="defaultList"><li><span style="display: unset;">Visual interpretation of temporal vegetation index profiles (e.g. NDVI)</span></li><li><span style="display: unset;">Collection of on screen validation data on historic crop types</span></li><li><span style="display: unset;">Collection of on screen validation data on historic land use</span></li><li><span style="display: unset;">Quality control and quality assurance</span></li><li><span style="display: unset;">Creation of maps and figures</span></li></ul> 
<p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span class="" style="display: unset;"><span style="display: unset;">The candidate ideally should have a training in remote sensing and should be able to work independently under the supervision of the TRANSECT team.</span> 
</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">General requirements:</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p> <ul class="defaultList"><li><span style="display: initial;">Good command of English</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Good knowledge of the mathematical/physical basics of remote sensing and the processing of satellite images</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">A good understanding of phenological characteristics of different crop types</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Practical experience in raster and vector data processing</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Confident handling of GIS software environments (preferably QGIS)</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">An independent, structured, goal-oriented and reliable way of working</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Ability to work in a team and good communication skills</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Ideally, the candidate should have practical experience in the programming environments R and/or Python</span></li></ul> 
<p><span style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">Further information:</span></p><p><span style="font-weight: bold; display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p> <ul class="defaultList"><li><span style="display: initial;">Appointment from July 1</span><sup style="display: initial;">st</sup><span style="display: initial;">, 2022</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">The position is initially limited to 6 month with an option for possible extension of 6 months</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">ca. 10 hours per week</span></li><li><span style="display: initial;">Payment according to public pay agreement</span></li></ul> 
<p><span style="display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span class="" style="display: initial;"><span style="display: initial;">The Student Assistant will be supervised by TRANSECT member Dr Christoph Raab, remote sensing and GIS researcher, who can be contacted for inquiries regarding the position. <br/>&nbsp;<br/>Further information about the project:</span> 
</span><a href="http://www.transect.de/" target="_blank" runtime_url="http://www.transect.de/" style="display: initial;">www.transect.de</a></p><p><span style="display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">The application should consist of a single PDF document containing a cover letter with a brief description of your possible starting date, your research background and interest, motivation, particular skills that you would like to highlight, and a short CV. <br/>&nbsp;<br/></span><span class="" style="display: initial; font-weight: bold;"><span style="display: initial; font-weight: bold;">Send your application until</span> 
</span><span style="display: initial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">May 31, 2022</span><span class="" style="display: initial; font-weight: bold;"> <span style="display: initial; font-weight: bold;">to:</span></span><span style="display: initial;"><br/>&nbsp;<br/></span><a href="file:///C:/Users/mmaehlis/Desktop/Christoph.Raab@hnee.de" target="_blank" style="display: initial;">Christoph.Raab@hnee.de</a></p><p><span style="display: initial;">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">Dr Christoph Raab</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">TRANSECT</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">Schwappachweg 3 (22.1)</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">16225 Eberswalde</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;">Germany</span></p><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p><p><span style="display: initial;"><br/></span></p></div> 
</div> 
